debug watchpoint <subcommand> [<arguments>]
  Possible subcommands are:
    list      list all active watchpoints
    create    create a new watchpoint
    configure configure an existing watchpoint
    remove    remove an existing watchpoint
  Type 'help debug watchpoint <subcommand>' for help about a specific subcommand.

debug watchpoint create [<property-name> <property-value>]...
  Create a new watchpoint with given properties. The following properties are supported:
  -type       one of 'read_io', 'write_io', 'read_mem', 'write_mem'
  -address    the address(es) where the watchpoint should trigger, can be a single address or a begin/end-pair
  -condition  a Tcl expression that must evaluate to true for the watchpoint to trigger (default = no condition)
  -command    a Tcl command that should be executed when the watchpoint triggers (default = 'debug break')
  -enabled    set to false to (temporarily) disable this watchpoint
  -once       if 'true' the watchpoint is automatically removed after it triggered (default = 'false', meaning recurring)

debug breakpoint create [<property-name> <property-value>]...
  Create a new breakpoint with given properties. The following properties are supported:
  -address    the address where the breakpoint should trigger
  -condition  a Tcl expression that must evaluate to true for the breakpoint to trigger (default = no condition)
  -command    a Tcl command that should be executed when the breakpoint triggers (default = 'debug break')
  -enabled    set to false to (temporarily) disable this breakpoint
  -once       if 'true' the breakpoint is automatically removed after it triggered (default = 'false', meaning recurring)

